{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}ROML core overhead — ROML model-build benchmark{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<h1>ROML Python scalar / bulk vs native Rust core</h1>
<p>Both ROML Python paths and the native core build mathematically identical
models: same variables, constraints, coefficients, bounds, objective, and
naming policy. The <strong>scalar-vs-scalar</strong> comparison isolates
Python/binding/modeling overhead most cleanly; the
<strong>bulk-vs-core</strong> comparison answers how close the public Python
fast path gets to native construction.</p>
{% for title, div in charts %}
<div class="chart"><h2>{{ title }}</h2>{{ div | safe }}</div>
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
